mp_hal_ticks_ms/us must be MONOTONIC; on Phoenix they were the wall clock.

Both functions select their clock with

    #if (defined(_POSIX_TIMERS) && _POSIX_TIMERS > 0) && defined(_POSIX_MONOTONIC_CLOCK)
        clock_gettime(CLOCK_MONOTONIC, ...)
    #else
        gettimeofday(...)          /* <-- Phoenix took this branch */
    #endif

libphoenix advertises _POSIX_VERSION 200809L but defines no POSIX *option*
macros at all, so that test is always false here and both tick functions fell
back to gettimeofday(). That is the wall clock: on Phoenix CLOCK_REALTIME is
CLOCK_MONOTONIC plus a settable offset (libphoenix time/time.c), so it steps
whenever anything calls clock_settime()/settimeofday() -- ntpclient does, at
boot.

These two are MicroPython's monotonic primitives. time.ticks_ms()/ticks_us()
and especially time.ticks_diff() are documented as monotonic and are the
standard way MicroPython code measures elapsed time; backing them with a
steppable clock makes ticks_diff() return nonsense (including negative or huge
values) across a clock set. Phoenix does support CLOCK_MONOTONIC, so ask for it
directly.

Same defect and same fix as the Quake II frame timer (phoenix-rtos-ports
4a166c4). Found by measuring which ports test the absent option macros:
docs/misc/2026-09-10-posix-option-macros-blast-radius.md in the coordination
repo. Guarded on __phoenix__ so other platforms keep the upstream probe.

--- micropython-1.26.0/ports/unix/unix_mphal.c	2026-09-10 08:29:20.974569040 +0200
+++ micropython-phoenix/ports/unix/unix_mphal.c	2026-09-10 08:29:20.984139513 +0200
@@ -206,7 +206,7 @@
 
 #ifndef mp_hal_ticks_ms
 mp_uint_t mp_hal_ticks_ms(void) {
-    #if (defined(_POSIX_TIMERS) && _POSIX_TIMERS > 0) && defined(_POSIX_MONOTONIC_CLOCK)
+    #if defined(__phoenix__) || ((defined(_POSIX_TIMERS) && _POSIX_TIMERS > 0) && defined(_POSIX_MONOTONIC_CLOCK))
     struct timespec tv;
     clock_gettime(CLOCK_MONOTONIC, &tv);
     return tv.tv_sec * 1000 + tv.tv_nsec / 1000000;
@@ -220,7 +220,7 @@
 
 #ifndef mp_hal_ticks_us
 mp_uint_t mp_hal_ticks_us(void) {
-    #if (defined(_POSIX_TIMERS) && _POSIX_TIMERS > 0) && defined(_POSIX_MONOTONIC_CLOCK)
+    #if defined(__phoenix__) || ((defined(_POSIX_TIMERS) && _POSIX_TIMERS > 0) && defined(_POSIX_MONOTONIC_CLOCK))
     struct timespec tv;
     clock_gettime(CLOCK_MONOTONIC, &tv);
     return tv.tv_sec * 1000000 + tv.tv_nsec / 1000;
